\begin{definition}[Natarajan Dimension]
The \emph{Natarajan Dimension} of a family $\H$ is the smallest $d$ such that for all concepts $h\in\H$, there exists a labeled sample of size $d$ that is consistent with $h$ and such that any other concept in $\H$ that is consistent with that sample satisfies $h\subset h'$.
\end{definition}

\begin{remark}
Natarajan proves that $VC \le E.ND$, and \cite{goldman1995complexity} prove that $ND\le TD$. \olivier{There seems to be a bug in this proof though!}
\end{remark}

